4. Chat templates and model data
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
No chat template is embedded in the engine. It renders the template stored in
the model's GGUF file (tokenizer.chat_template), or a template file the user
passes with --template. Model weights, templates and tokenizer data come with
the model under its publisher's terms and are not covered by this project's
LGPL grant.

The test fixtures in fixtures/ contain small excerpts of DiffusionGemma-26B-A4B-it
material, which Google publishes under the Apache License 2.0
(https://huggingface.co/google/diffusiongemma-26B-A4B-it, revision
f7f5b7f5fa82ffc52addd066915886d497f5517b), and of Unsloth's GGUF conversion of it
(https://huggingface.co/unsloth/diffusiongemma-26B-A4B-it-GGUF, revision
f4183a2c7a354128d02545752303c4354d165bf0):

- fixtures/generation_config.json: a copy of the model's generation configuration;
- fixtures/chat/gemma4_canonical.jinja: the model's chat_template.jinja;
- fixtures/chat/gemma4_unsloth_gguf.jinja: the chat template stored in the GGUF;
- fixtures/chat/gemma4_chat_reference.json, fixtures/output/gemma4_output_cases.json:
  prompts rendered with those templates, token IDs and token strings;
- fixtures/quantized/*.rows: a few quantized weight rows from the GGUF, with
  derived reference outputs.

These excerpts remain under the Apache License 2.0
(https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0) and are used only by the tests.

